**Read:** [Phase Transitions — Bhadeshia and Yan](../sources/Phase-Transitions-Bhadeshia-Yan.lingua#r_2PMPJ2B4GPGDT62S567TX1DCPJ), the entire nucleation and precipitation chapters with their worked examples; [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), the complete aluminium/precipitation and advanced transformation notes; [Mechanical Behavior of Materials — Krystyn Van Vliet, MIT 3.22](../sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC), the full particle/structure-strengthening context.

Precipitation involves a driving force, interfacial/strain contributions, nucleation, growth, diffusion, and possibly a sequence of metastable states. A stable equilibrium phase diagram does not automatically identify the first phase formed or the particle population controlling early properties.

Distinguish particle fraction, number, size/shape distribution, chemistry, coherence, spacing, and location. Growth/coarsening and solute depletion can alter strengthening, stability, corrosion, and later transformation. A peak hardness time in one specimen/thermal history is not a universal treatment for all dimensions and initial states.

Use consistent material and solute balances. Compare transformation/precipitation measurements, calorimetry, microscopy/diffraction, and property response with their actual resolution and histories. A fitted kinetic exponent or coarsening coefficient can combine assumptions and missing mechanisms; independent evidence is needed for interpretation.

**Work:** read the complete precipitation chapter and reconstruct a full primary alloy-aging study. Derive a governing nucleation/growth or coarsening relation, independently check a limiting/balance case, and compare models against separate structural and property observations. Test an alternative initial state or thermal history and explain which measurement most discriminates the mechanisms. Later processing/project work combines the result with fabrication and service requirements.

**Continue:** [Test transformation models against phase, spatial, and time-dependent evidence](Transformation-kinetics-nucleation-growth-and-competing-mechanisms.lingua#r_454J0PMVBRQA4PQ3SHE6E7JKDE).

**Return:** [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).
